  {
   "type": "events",
   "id": "589331",
   "attributes": {
    "id": 589331,
    "title": "IEEE PES ESPAÑA | [Webinar #2 - 09.11.2026] | Cybersecurity of Control Room of the Future using Artificial Intelligence",
    "description": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span lang=\"ES\">Cap&iacute;tulo Espa&ntilde;ol IEEE/PES</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Estimados miembros del Cap&iacute;tulo:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Se remite informaci&oacute;n de un nuevo seminario, esperando que sea de vuestro inter&eacute;s.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Un saludo,</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Jos&eacute; Mar&iacute;a Maza Ortega,&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"ES\">Presidente Cap&iacute;tulo Espa&ntilde;ol de IEEE/PES</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">&nbsp;--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">T&iacute;tulo: </span><strong><span lang=\"EN\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Cybersecurity of Control Room of the Future using Artificial Intelligence</span></span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN\">Ponente: Dr. Alex Stefanov, TU Delft<span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\">, The Netherlands</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Resumen:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Electrical power grids are vulnerable to cyber attacks, as seen in Ukraine in and 2022, 2016, and 2015. These cyber attacks are classified as Advanced Persistent Threats (APTs) posing serious threats to power grid operation from Control Room of the Future (CRoF), potentially causing cascading failures and wide-spread blackouts. However, state-of-the-art intrusion detection systems and mitigation techniques are inadequate for APT detection and prevention owing to their stealthy nature and long-lasting persistence. Furthermore, they are ineffective as they focus on individual anomaly instances and overlook the correlation between attack instances. In this seminar, we analyse the emerging cyber security threats for power systems. We will discuss how APTs on Operational Technologies (OT) networks in CRoF and digital substations can cause cascading failures and continental blackouts. Solutions using AI are discussed to strengthen the cyber security of CRoF. AI-based methods will be presented for spatio-temporal APT detection and correlation for cyber-physical power systems from CRoF. They provide online situational awareness for power system operators to pinpoint power system-wide anomaly locations in near real-time and pre-emptively mitigate APTs using preventive controlled islanding at an early stage before causing adverse impacts. A CRoF cyber range infrastructure is presented for joint attack / defence exercises and training of power grid operators in CRoF and cyber security professionals in Security Operation Centers (SOC) to cooperatively detect and mitigate APTs and increase the cyber security and cyber resilience of power grids</span></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Lugar: Videconferencia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Idioma: Ingl&eacute;s</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Fecha: Lunes, 9 de noviembre de 2026<br>Hora: 18:00 - 19:30 (CET)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Webinar gratuito</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Registro: <a href=\"https://events.vtools.ieee.org/event/register/589331\">https://events.vtools.ieee.org/event/register/589331</a></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Cierre registro: 06.11.2026 a las 11:00 AM (CET)&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Nota: El registro es obligatorio para recibir el enlace URL del evento, que ser&aacute; enviado el mismo d&iacute;a del evento a las 13:00 (CET). La participaci&oacute;n en esta actividad es gratuita y abierta a cualquier asistente, incluyendo miembros de IEEE/PES y no miembros, por lo que puede compartir el enlace de esta noticia.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"ES\">Enlace a la noticia:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://events.vtools.ieee.org/m/589331\">https://events.vtools.ieee.org/m/589331</a></span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
